From: OneKiwi <support@onekiwi.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: v4l2-async: Fix NULL pointer dereference in match_fwnode

When a virtual or platform subdev without a firmware node (sd->fwnode is NULL,
such as soc_sensor in Mali-C55 ISP) is registered, match_fwnode() is called
against existing notifiers.
Evaluating sd->fwnode->secondary causes a kernel NULL pointer dereference crash.
Fix this by checking !sd->fwnode before accessing sd->fwnode->secondary.

--- a/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-async.c
+++ b/drivers/media/v4l2-core/v4l2-async.c
@@ -153,7 +153,7 @@ static bool match_fwnode(struct v4l2_async_notifier *notifier,
 		return true;
 
 	/* Also check the secondary fwnode. */
-	if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(sd->fwnode->secondary))
+	if (!sd->fwnode || IS_ERR_OR_NULL(sd->fwnode->secondary))
 		return false;
 
 	return match_fwnode_one(notifier, sd, sd->fwnode->secondary, asd);
